Checks the D word start angle offset for spindle synchronized motion.

Covers that the angle reaches the canon layer for both G33 and G76, that it is
absent (and so defaults to zero) when no D is programmed, and that a negative D
is passed on as its magnitude rather than being dropped.

The G76 case uses an entry taper (L1) on purpose: that makes a single threading
pass emit more than one synchronized move, which is the case where the offset
has to be applied only once, at the index pulse, rather than at the start of
every segment of the pass.
